  "scope": "Test native FP32 matmul preservation and explicit rounding counterfactuals.\n\nSeeded synthetic matrices, not learned attention or complete-model attribution.\nIdentity operands remain dynamic native inputs. All inputs and outputs use\nFP32 storage; some cases intentionally contain exactly BF16-representable values.\n",
  "finding": "On seeded FP32 matrices, native multiplication by a dynamic identity operand matches ten-fraction-bit TF32 truncation bitwise and differs0.00041749 from the original input. BF16-representable values in FP32 storage survive identity bitwise. Random FP32 product error is0.00171543; after CPU input-truncation counterfactual it remains0.00107494. Random BF16-representable product error is0.00074521. Thus the identity proves a precision limit for that operation, while simple input/output rounding alone does not explain general matrix error. All native operations use HiFi4/FP32 operands and accumulation, exact repeats and no fallback.",
